es that they represented when  vegeta arrives he doesn't show affection  for his allies or anyone really in fact  he kills his oldest comrade the second  he's no longer useful to him in this way  vegeta acts as the opposite of what goku  represents in the story having given up  his life at the beginning of the arc to  save literally everyone goku travels to  otherworld and after exerting more  effort than any mortal in history across  snake way requests the help of someone  he has never met so that he can continue  to defend others and once he touches  down on the battlefield having been  brought back by his friends he finds  himself as the one thing standing  between everything he cares about and  certain annihilation all with the  technique that he managed to acquire  thanks to the philosophy he believed in  in this way battle shonen has  facilitated not only a beam struggle but  a struggle of ideology between ego and  humility the beam struggle wasn't a  cornerstone moment in a battle that has  gone down in history as one of the  greatest of all times simply because it  looked visually interesting absolutely  not it's because of what it represents  and so across the series techniques like  the spirit bomb kaioken and kamehameha  didn't just look cool through their  acquisition or connection to the story  they each represented a part of goku's  identity and in that same way during  this battle with gara naruto's  philosophy and way of life is challenged  directly by his natural opposite ingara  and to combat this natural opposing  threat naruto uses the techniques that  represent who he is and what makes him a  terrific character after overcoming the  initial shock that came from confronting  a demented and psychotic version of  himself early on in the conflict a tried  and true means of building up tension to  a big reveal took place gara would knock  naruto to the floor berating him and  poking what he saw as holes in his  idealistic and hopeful outlook on life 